       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order, because the dose looks like an error.\n\n**Why I stopped:** Metformin 2550 mg three times daily comes to **7,650 mg/day**. The maximum recommended daily dose for adults is **2,550 mg/day** (some references say 2,000 mg/day for extended-release). This order is three times that, which risks severe lactic acidosis and GI toxicity.\n\n**What you may have meant:** 2550 mg is the total daily maximum. Divided three times daily with meals, that would be **850 mg PO TID**.\n\n**Also worth checking:** Metformin is usually started low, for example 500 mg once or twice daily with meals, and titrated up over weeks to limit GI side effects. If this patient is new to metformin, a starting dose may fit better than the maximum.\n\nPlease tell me which of these you want:\n1. **850 mg PO TID with meals** (2,550 mg/day)\n2. A lower starting or titration dose, such as 500 mg PO BID with meals\n3. Another dose, if you confirm 2550 mg per dose is what you intend. I'd suggest checking with your resident or attending or the pharmacist first.\n\nI can enter the order once you confirm."
      }
     ],
